  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"2.1.16\"\n\npackage:\n  name: pyglet\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/p/pyglet/pyglet-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: ca90ee05532ced8330b8a8087ac2a7b69589b7fa7fb67f85aabe24aaf4ae42c0\n  patches:\n    # FFmpeg 9 support, https://github.com/pyglet/pyglet/pull/1499\n    - 0001-Add-compatibility-for-ffmpeg-9.0.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - pip\n    - flit-core >=3.2,<4\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - freetype\n    # pyglet only knows the FFmpeg 4-9 library names (avutil-56 .. avutil-61);\n    # 9 is supported through the backported patch\n    - ffmpeg >=4.0.0,<10\n    - if: linux\n      then: __linux\n    - if: osx\n      then: __osx\n    - if: win\n      then: __win\n    # pyglet dlopens the unversioned libGL.so, which only libgl-devel provides\n    - if: linux\n      then: libgl-devel\n\ntests:\n  # All \"import ...\" tests live in `run_tests.py`. Imports that need a\n  # display are skipped on Linux, so no (virtual) X server is required.\n  - files:\n      recipe:\n        - run_tests.py\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - if: linux\n          then: libglu\n        - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - pip\n    script:\n      - pip check\n      - python run_tests.py\n\nabout:\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: Cross-platform windowing and multimedia library\n  homepage: http://pyglet.org\n  repository: https://github.com/pyglet/pyglet\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - mwcraig\n    - jakirkham\n    - bitcraft\n    - hmaarrfk  # just a maintainer to help move things forward. Happy to retire myself\n",
